# ═══ META-LESSONS ═══
L1: The P1 stand-down architect contract is a FEATURE, not a bug. The Void return (solver.rs:999-1003) makes the Stub backend FAIL-CLOSED — callers can distinguish 'no proof' from 'fake proof'. This is documented at solver.rs:999-1003 and the contract is correct.

L2: The 0.85 bump is honest. The EXECUTABLE-CONTRACTS half (change-contract) and the SMT-PROOFS half (cli_prove_claim + z3 backend) are BOTH live. The 'arbitrary type-theoretic' half is a separate Lean/Coq epic — different solver class entirely (tactic prover vs SMT solver).

L3: When a wave is declared 10ed but the substrate is already 95% there, the right move is: VERIFY + DOCUMENT + BUMP SPEC, not invent new engineering. P3-NOOP audit pattern: ALWAYS check the actual code state before claiming SHIPPED.

L4: The 10ed budget was 5-10x more than the 0.5ed reality. The P1+P4 wave was effectively a VERIFICATION wave. This is fine — the spec bump moves the substrate from "claimed but unverified" to "verified at 0.85".

L5: PARCIAL=0 is a HISTORIC MILESTONE. The CAH roadmap TIER 1-3 is now CLOSED. The only remaining rows are 2 AUSENTE (multimodal non-goal + 1 A-prefix).
